  "measurement": {
    "chrome": "Only capture probes whether to install the product relay. The trace lacks that result. A specific Chrome capture cold install is not directly distinguished by its complete row. Ordinary commit always dispatches to the existing relay and reads its own nonce-matched receipt.",
    "direct": "The archived process diagnostic contains per-command action, request digest, sequence, complete phase and transportSucceeded. The two original SQLite backups also contain a matching durable START.",
    "edge": "Before capture, the combined preparation must bind the foreground original. Every successful original Edge capture includes its own native script-URL witness submission, a verified return from the actual confirm check, separate current-target validation and a positive capture command receipt. Emitting armed also requires admission of the typed target, binding to its relay, retained witness and a current foreground scheduler epoch.",
    "negativeControl": "Edge selection sequence 60 reached the receipt phase and rejected this individual capture with pageRejected(CLICK_PIN_REFUSED). Its earlier witness confirmation, validation and submission had already run. There is no successful capture result for this event.",
    "proofGrade": "The Edge confirm return is compelled by the recorded complete event and the frozen executable control flow. There is no dedicated logged confirm return, browser engine context ID or provider object in the trace.",
    "siteRealm": "The Edge product witness confirms a per-document distinction and expected round trip. Neither product command success nor a second QA view of the original DOM and its own XHR constructor identifies the actual website upload object, body, progress or terminal status.",
    "successfulReceiptSemantics": "After submission, the executor can record complete only after the same command nonce and positive result envelope passed validation, process identity remained current and size limits passed. The raw envelope, nonce, OS descriptor and return text are absent. Subsequent typed observations establish application-level consequences.",
    "traceAuthority": "The opt-in diagnostics originate from the signed executable. Their stored bytes are pinned here by SHA-256. Individual diagnostic events do not carry independent cryptographic signatures."
  },
